{
  "reconstructed_theorem_text": "E_n=EuclideanSpace R (Fin(n+1)), the real (n+1)-coordinate space with its l2 Euclidean norm. Let S_n={z in E_n: ||z||=1}, considered as a subtype when it is used as a carrier. Let C_(n,N)=Fin N -> S_n. For each n,N:Nat, the target definition is the function type C_(n,N)=Fin N -> S_n. Thus a configuration assigns one unit vector to each index. Neither n nor N is required positive; N=0 gives the empty-index function type. This defines a carrier and does not itself assert differentiability, probability or a product geometric metric.",
